WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.626
Bearing diagnosis becomes harder when speed, load, or interference changes.

00:00:05.816 --> 00:00:12.258
These conditions alter the measured vibration, even when the underlying fault category stays the same.

00:00:12.448 --> 00:00:20.702
This study asks how physically meaningful structure can organize complementary representations for more robust diagnosis.

00:00:22.108 --> 00:00:25.958
A localized bearing fault leaves several related signatures.

00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:34.766
Transient impacts appear in time, characteristic patterns appear in time and frequency, and recurring behavior is tied to rotation.

00:00:34.956 --> 00:00:39.722
The method treats these views as related evidence from the same fault process.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.534
Physical information enters before and during learning.

00:00:44.724 --> 00:00:56.040
Rotational information guides how recurring structure is represented, while bearing geometry and speed provide references for diagnostically relevant frequency regions.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:02.843
The physical guidance is at the representation and architecture levels; it is not a physics-residual loss.

00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:08.427
The views are coordinated rather than merely collected independently.

00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:16.606
Time-frequency evidence provides complementary guidance to temporal modeling, while the original temporal information path is retained.

00:01:16.796 --> 00:01:25.381
Learned fusion then adjusts the contributions of the views, limiting dependence on any single potentially degraded representation.

00:01:26.775 --> 00:01:29.636
The evaluation separates different questions.

00:01:29.826 --> 00:01:33.793
Raw-signal noise tests examine interference robustness.

00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:42.132
Complete held-out records test unseen operating conditions without target-condition data in training or model selection.

00:01:42.322 --> 00:01:49.734
Experiments using labeled target data are reported separately as adaptation, not target-free generalization.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:55.396
The findings support complementary evidence in demanding settings.

00:01:55.586 --> 00:02:04.629
The temporal path provides useful support under strong noise, and the full framework performs well in the evaluated target-free operating shifts.

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:12.519
Clean classification is already near saturation, so that result alone cannot establish a broad superiority claim.

00:02:13.942 --> 00:02:23.423
The contribution is a physically organized multi-representation framework, connecting signal construction, cross-view interaction, and learned fusion.

00:02:23.613 --> 00:02:35.121
Component studies and representation audits examine the role of these choices, while distinct protocols clarify which claims concern noise, generalization, or adaptation.

00:02:36.525 --> 00:02:45.302
The main conclusion is that physically organized complementary evidence can support robust diagnosis in the evaluated conditions.

00:02:45.492 --> 00:02:49.491
The speed assumption applies to short, approximately steady windows.

00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:58.512
Rapid acceleration and more varied field interference require further validation; the study does not claim universal robustness.
